[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854853715","pull_request_review_id":2455938140,"id":1854853715,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5ujtJT","diff_hunk":"@@ -825,7 +825,7 @@ class RenderingDeviceDriverD3D12 : public RenderingDeviceDriver {\n \t};\n \n public:\n-\tvirtual RenderPassID render_pass_create(VectorView<Attachment> p_attachments, VectorView<Subpass> p_subpasses, VectorView<SubpassDependency> p_subpass_dependencies, uint32_t p_view_count) override final;\n+\tvirtual RenderPassID render_pass_create(VectorView<Attachment> p_attachments, VectorView<Subpass> p_subpasses, VectorView<SubpassDependency> p_subpass_dependencies, uint32_t p_view_count, AttachmentReference p_fragment_density_map_attachment) override final;","path":"drivers/d3d12/rendering_device_driver_d3d12.h","commit_id":"76d709be74d6fa76ec3cd22af24e74b4b93602eb","original_commit_id":"6fda94006d7ce3595265d0e7dd5b77865478c3af","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@DarioSamo , I think we can make an improvement here by always requiring the fragment density map attachment to be passed through like this. Yes it's a feature of the KHR FRS extension that we can set the density map on each subpass, but in practice for our only use case, the mobile renderer using multiple subpasses, I think we can make the argument that we ALWAYS add the fragment density map to each subpass if FRS is used.\r\n\r\nThis would simplify the logic further on in the rendering engine and allow us to remove some of the enhancements around adding VRS attachments to subpasses. It will likely also make supporting Metal and DirectX easier as we won't need to make further checks whether those need to pass the attachment per subpass or as an extra parameter here.","created_at":"2024-11-22T23:00:52Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T23:01:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99551#discussion_r1854853715","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99551","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854853715"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99551#discussion_r1854853715"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99551"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854853715/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":828,"original_line":828,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":32,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854861300","pull_request_review_id":2455950991,"id":1854861300,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5uju_0","diff_hunk":"@@ -5642,14 +5709,22 @@ uint64_t RenderingDeviceDriverVulkan::limit_get(Limit p_limit) {\n \t\t\treturn subgroup_capabilities.supported_stages_flags_rd();\n \t\tcase LIMIT_SUBGROUP_OPERATIONS:\n \t\t\treturn subgroup_capabilities.supported_operations_flags_rd();\n-\t\tcase LIMIT_VRS_TEXEL_WIDTH:\n-\t\t\treturn vrs_capabilities.texel_size.x;\n-\t\tcase LIMIT_VRS_TEXEL_HEIGHT:\n-\t\t\treturn vrs_capabilities.texel_size.y;\n-\t\tcase LIMIT_VRS_MAX_FRAGMENT_WIDTH:\n-\t\t\treturn vrs_capabilities.max_fragment_size.x;\n-\t\tcase LIMIT_VRS_MAX_FRAGMENT_HEIGHT:\n-\t\t\treturn vrs_capabilities.max_fragment_size.y;\n+\t\tcase LIMIT_FRAGMENT_SHADING_RATE_TEXEL_WIDTH:","path":"drivers/vulkan/rendering_device_driver_vulkan.cpp","commit_id":"76d709be74d6fa76ec3cd22af24e74b4b93602eb","original_commit_id":"6fda94006d7ce3595265d0e7dd5b77865478c3af","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Does it make sense to split these into two groups? I guess its needed if we allow both extensions to be enabled, but I think it can be a valid restriction that we enable only one. ","created_at":"2024-11-22T23:03:54Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T23:42:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99551#discussion_r1854861300","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99551","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854861300"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99551#discussion_r1854861300"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99551"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854861300/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":5712,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":338,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854869243","pull_request_review_id":2455950991,"id":1854869243,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5ujw77","diff_hunk":"@@ -103,8 +109,16 @@ void VRS::copy_vrs(RID p_source_rd_texture, RID p_dest_framebuffer, bool p_multi\n }\n \n Size2i VRS::get_vrs_texture_size(const Size2i p_base_size) const {\n-\tint32_t texel_width = RD::get_singleton()->limit_get(RD::LIMIT_VRS_TEXEL_WIDTH);\n-\tint32_t texel_height = RD::get_singleton()->limit_get(RD::LIMIT_VRS_TEXEL_HEIGHT);\n+\tint32_t texel_width = 0;\n+\tint32_t texel_height = 0;\n+\tif (RD::get_singleton()->has_feature(RD::SUPPORTS_FRAGMENT_DENSITY_MAP)) {","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/effects/vrs.cpp","commit_id":"76d709be74d6fa76ec3cd22af24e74b4b93602eb","original_commit_id":"6fda94006d7ce3595265d0e7dd5b77865478c3af","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"So this kind of bolts down to a design choice that I do know the right way forward for and ties into remarks I made in earlier comments.\r\n\r\nEspecially once Metal and DirectX come into play, we're starting to make a lot of GPU specific choices outside of our driver that will make code like in these spots more and more complex. If we can we should internalise these choices.\r\n\r\nAlso we're making the assumption here that if the density map extension is available, thats the choice we're going with. That may be true for the Quest (where this enables performance improvements), but there is no telling if this is universally true. It is very possible that on other hardware we should prioritise the KHR over the EXT if both are available.\r\n\r\nI think we should have a way to indirect which one is prefered, where at initialisation either one or the other is enabled, and on calling `RD::get_singleton()->limit_get(RD::LIMIT_VRS_TEXEL_WIDTH);` we return the correct value for the extension we use. And it will be future proof for when we have Metal and/or DirectX support.\r\n\r\nThis also ensures that we don't accidentally mix and match logic, we get a consistent choice made by the rendering driver.\r\n\r\nWe can't get away with some querying and specific logic (like whether our density map has rates or weights and whether X and Y are split into channels) but also that requirement can be queried from the rendering driver which then returns the correct requirements based on the chosen extension.","created_at":"2024-11-22T23:14:20Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T23:42:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99551#discussion_r1854869243","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99551","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854869243"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99551#discussion_r1854869243"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99551"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854869243/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":114,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":44,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854872602","pull_request_review_id":2455950991,"id":1854872602,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5ujxwa","diff_hunk":"@@ -172,6 +172,7 @@ RID RenderForwardMobile::RenderBufferDataForwardMobile::get_color_fbs(Framebuffe\n \n \tuint32_t view_count = render_buffers->get_view_count();\n \n+\tbool vrs_uses_fdm = RD::get_singleton()->has_feature(RD::SUPPORTS_FRAGMENT_DENSITY_MAP);","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_mobile/render_forward_mobile.cpp","commit_id":"76d709be74d6fa76ec3cd22af24e74b4b93602eb","original_commit_id":"6fda94006d7ce3595265d0e7dd5b77865478c3af","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"So just to hark back on my earlier remark up above. If we go for an API that always specifies a VRS attachment on the pass, and we just apply it to all subpasses, instead of adding an attachment to each subpass here, we can simplify this logic and not have to make choices here which may also end up being different on Metal and/or DirectX.\r\n\r\nIf we do keep the current approach of adding attachments to subpasses here, I think the constant passed here should be more generic, like `RD::SUPPORT_VRS_PER_SUBPASS` that switches whether we can specify a density map per subpass instead of supplying one for the whole pass.","created_at":"2024-11-22T23:18:19Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T23:42:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99551#discussion_r1854872602","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99551","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854872602"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99551#discussion_r1854872602"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99551"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854872602/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":175,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854874575","pull_request_review_id":2455950991,"id":1854874575,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5ujyPP","diff_hunk":"@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ class FramebufferCacheRD : public Object {\n \n \tstatic _FORCE_INLINE_ uint32_t _hash_pass(const RD::FramebufferPass &p, uint32_t h) {\n \t\th = hash_murmur3_one_32(p.depth_attachment, h);\n-\t\th = hash_murmur3_one_32(p.vrs_attachment, h);\n+\t\th = hash_murmur3_one_32(p.fragment_shading_rate_attachment, h);","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/framebuffer_cache_rd.h","commit_id":"76d709be74d6fa76ec3cd22af24e74b4b93602eb","original_commit_id":"6fda94006d7ce3595265d0e7dd5b77865478c3af","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think this should remain being named `vrs_attachment`, we're painting ourselves into a corner if Metal or DirectX or some other future extension also allows the density map to be specified per subpass, when we start naming variables in the `renderer_rd` based off of differences in Vulkan extensions. ","created_at":"2024-11-22T23:20:27Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T23:42:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99551#discussion_r1854874575","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99551","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854874575"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99551#discussion_r1854874575"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99551"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854874575/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":62,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1854875396","pull_request_review_id":2455950991,"id":1854875396,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5ujycE","diff_hunk":"@@ -1424,7 +1424,7 @@ void RendererSceneRenderRD::sdfgi_set_debug_probe_select(const Vector3 &p_positi\n RendererSceneRenderRD *RendererSceneRenderRD::singleton = nullptr;\n \n bool RendererSceneRenderRD::is_vrs_supported() const {\n-\treturn RD::get_singleton()->has_feature(RD::SUPPORTS_ATTACHMENT_VRS);\n+\treturn RD::get_singleton()->has_feature(RD::SUPPORTS_ATTACHMENT_FRAGMENT_SHADING_RATE) || RD::get_singleton()->has_feature(RD::SUPPORTS_FRAGMENT_DENSITY_MAP);","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/renderer_scene_render_rd.cpp","commit_id":"76d709be74d6fa76ec3cd22af24e74b4b93602eb","original_commit_id":"6fda94006d7ce3595265d0e7dd5b77865478c3af","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0N